{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "bounded_regret_local",
  "intent": "Primary signal is current distance (local_distance family). The bounded regret term `0.25 * regret / (1 + 0.5 * distance)` adds a secondary preference for isolated candidates (large gap between nearest and second-nearest unvisited). The denominator dampens regret when the candidate is already close, preventing zigzagging. This differs from seed regret_aware by making the regret contribution distance-dependent rather than linear-constant.",
  "tags": [
    "local_distance",
    "regret"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['regret']\n    den = max(1e-9, 1.0 + 0.5 * d)\n    p = -d + 0.25 * r / den\n    return p",
